 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Talk about plans",
   "texto": [
    "For nearby plans the **presente** is very common with a word of time: **Domani vado a Roma** (tomorrow I go to Rome), **Stasera guardo un film** (tonight I see a movie). **Andare a + infinitivo** often expresses movement or intention to do something (**Vado a comprare il pane** = I will buy bread); depending on the context it can also refer to a near future, but it is not the general equivalent of any Spanish future.",
    "Useful words: **domani** (tomorrow), **stasera** (tonight), **questo fine settimana**, **la settimana prossima** (next week). **Andare a trovare** means visiting someone."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Invite and respond",
   "texto": [
    "**Vuoi venire?** (do you want to come?). More colloquial: **Ti va di venire?** (would you like to come?).",
    "To accept: **Volentieri!** (with pleasure!) or **Buona idea!** To reject: **Mi dispiace, non posso**. To express agreement or disagreement: **Sono d'accordo** (I agree), **Non sono d'accordo** (I disagree).",
    "To stay: **Ci vediamo alle otto** (see you at 8: 00)."
   ]
  },
